# Patterns here are rooted at the build context: `node_modules` alone would
# match only a top-level directory, so anything that can appear below the
# root is written with `**/`.

# Secrets and local state. Never in an image, and never in the context a
# remote builder receives. This also keeps a local web/.env out of the client
# build, which must take its values from build arguments alone.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.sqlite3

# Environments, dependencies and caches, all rebuilt inside the image.
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# The client is built inside the image from its sources; a local build or its
# incremental state must not stand in for that.
web/dist/
web/*.tsbuildinfo

# Not part of the served application.
.git
.github/
.claude/
contracts/
tests/
agents/
docs/
notes/

# Each edition's free tier is served under /app/editions/, so it enters the
# context -- by name, and nothing else in that directory. editions/README.md
# tells a seat holder to put the dataset they bought there to hash it, and a
# deploy sends the working tree, not the commit.
editions/*
!editions/edition-*-sample.html
!editions/edition-*-sample.json
!editions/edition-*-manifest.json
